      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. it's a good start, but it's a bit too high-level. can you expand on each section? i need specific protocols for each unit, like what they should do first, second, and third when they arrive on scene. \n\nalso, just looking at the draft, the urgency score is sitting pretty low. like, it's basically a zero right now. i know i said don't spam it, but during an actual drill, the dispatchers really need to feel the weight of the situation when they see the doc. can you try to make the tone feel a bit more 'high-stakes' without losing the clarity? try to incorporate some of those urgency terms where they actually make sense in a professional context so the score isn't so low.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
